{
  "slug": "smdd-toolkit",
  "name": "Smdd Toolkit",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Structured Markdown Driven Development is a relaxed, controlled, and close to natural language programming paradigm. It is how the future of development looks like.  These are skills for Claude Code. Projects are markdown files, code is generated by claude (smdd-compile). CC builds component-by-component with atomic, parallel-safe sub-agents.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **4 skills**.\n\n- **Skills** (4): `smdd` (Use this skill when the user mentions SMDD (Structured Markdown Driven Development), asks to \"plan in SMDD style,\"…), `smdd-check` (Folder-level coherence audit for an SMDD project), `smdd-code` (Atomic WORK task for building one SMDD component), `smdd-compile` (Orchestrator that builds a batch of SMDD components with parallel sub-agents)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install smdd-toolkit@claude-community` from `cyvnrs/smdd-toolkit`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
    "codex"
  ],
  "pluginType": "wrapper",
  "wrapper": "skill",
  "sourceType": "community",
